{
 "_comment": [
  "Which HSK/CEFR level each grammar point belongs to.",
  "",
  "The Chinese Grammar Wiki builds its level tables with Semantic",
  "MediaWiki queries, so the list of points per level exists only in",
  "the rendered index pages -- and the wiki is behind a Cloudflare",
  "challenge that answers every request with HTTP 403. The Internet",
  "Archive has snapshots of those eight index pages, but it",
  "rate-limits hard enough that a fresh clone cannot be sure of",
  "getting them.",
  "",
  "So the mapping is kept here, in version control. It was read from",
  "the archive snapshots of the eight level index pages, and it is",
  "checked against the mirror: the mirror's own category tags agree",
  "with this file for every point that has both.",
  "",
  "The value is the list of level pages the point appears on:",
  "",
  "    A1, A2, B1, B2, C1   the CEFR level",
  "    HSK_1, HSK_2, HSK_3 the HSK level",
  "",
  "A point can appear under both, which is what the wiki does.",
  "",
  "This file is content, not code, and it is refreshed by",
  "pipeline/04_build_grammar.py --refresh-levels."
 ],
